OL,3,GNEWSAVillagers' emotion at Remembrance
OL,4,Apoppy response
OL,5,
OL,6,FThousands of poppies handcrafted by
OL,7,Fvillagers have been attached to a
OL,8,Fchurch wall in Wombourne for
OL,9,FRemembrance Day.
OL,11,FOrganiser Donna Eccleston said the size
OL,12,Fof the response to the project she
OL,13,Fstarted with fellow Wombourne Women's
OL,14,FInstitute member, Helen Standish-Bevan,
OL,15,Ftook her breath away.
OL,17,FOriginally they hoped to cover the
OL,18,Fvillage cenotaph, but they received so
OL,19,Fmany felt, knitted, crocheted and clay
OL,20,Fdonations, they now cover an outer wall
OL,21,Fand grounds of St Benedict Biscop
OL,22,FChurch in the village.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
